{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "diagram_type": "architecture",
  "meta": {
    "title": "One plugin tool, two roads to an agent",
    "subtitle": "Registered once in the kernel; reaches Codex natively and every ACP agent over a socket",
    "output": "docs/diagrams/plugin-tools.html"
  },
  "layout": {
    "mode": "grid",
    "origin": [
      60,
      120
    ],
    "cols": 4,
    "gapX": 40,
    "gapY": 62,
    "cellW": 168,
    "cellH": 66
  },
  "components": [
    {
      "id": "tool",
      "type": "backend",
      "label": "plugin tool",
      "sublabel": "registered once, in the kernel",
      "row": 0,
      "col": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "projection",
      "type": "backend",
      "label": "ToolProjection",
      "sublabel": "adapter-codex",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "codex",
      "type": "external",
      "label": "Codex",
      "sublabel": "dynamic tools on thread/start",
      "row": 2,
      "col": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "gateway",
      "type": "security",
      "label": "tool gateway",
      "sublabel": "one fs-permissioned socket",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "mcp",
      "type": "messagebus",
      "label": "packages/mcp-tools",
      "sublabel": "stdio MCP server",
      "row": 2,
      "col": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "acp",
      "type": "external",
      "label": "ACP agents",
      "sublabel": "Claude Code, Cursor, \u2026",
      "row": 3,
      "col": 2
    }
  ],
  "connections": [
    {
      "from": "tool",
      "to": "projection",
      "variant": "emphasis"
    },
    {
      "from": "projection",
      "to": "codex"
    },
    {
      "from": "tool",
      "to": "gateway",
      "variant": "emphasis"
    },
    {
      "from": "mcp",
      "to": "gateway",
      "label": "tools/list, tools/invoke",
      "variant": "security",
      "labelDy": -14
    },
    {
      "from": "acp",
      "to": "mcp",
      "label": "session/new mcpServers",
      "labelDy": -14
    }
  ],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why two roads and not one",
      "items": [
        "Codex takes tools directly, so it gets them with no broker",
        "ACP has no such channel \u2014 the gateway is how it reaches them",
        "A plugin author writes neither road; the tool is registered once"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What the socket costs",
      "items": [
        "NDJSON JSON-RPC over one unix socket in the state directory",
        "File permissions are the boundary; nothing is on a port",
        "Two verbs only, so a bridge cannot widen its own reach"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
